Chapter: DeckCellContract
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The deck is not a region. It is a watermark inside the same bump heap:
 `build` saves the heap position, records it with `__deck-set`, and
 advances past the reservation, and `phase-compact` is
 `__heap-restore (__deck-pos)`, so everything below the mark survives a
 compaction and everything above it is reclaimed. Three cells carry all
 of that state, and this asks whether they exist on the lane under test.

 It is a CONTRACT test rather than a survival test on purpose. Asking the
 survival question directly means calling `__heap-restore (__deck-pos)`,
 and on a lane where `__deck-pos` answers a literal zero that sets the
 allocation pointer to zero and takes the rest of the program with it. A
 lane that has not got the cells must fail this READABLY rather than
 crash, because a crash is the one result that cannot be told apart from
 the next defect along.

Section: Instrument

  show-yn : Boolean -> Text
  show-yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

Section: Report

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   let base = __heap-save
   in let marked = __deck-set base
   in let pos-after-set = __deck-pos
   in let p = __deck-alloc 64
   in let pos-after-alloc = __deck-pos
   in print-line-uni ("deck-set records the mark  : " & show-yn (pos-after-set == base))
   print-line-uni ("deck-alloc answers the mark: " & show-yn (p == base))
   print-line-uni ("deck-alloc bumps by size   : " & show-yn (pos-after-alloc - pos-after-set == 64))
   print-line-uni ("mark is not a literal zero : " & show-yn (pos-after-set > 0))
  end
